WRITING RULES (apply identically to every locale):
- FORMAT: Continuous prose in paragraphs only. Lists or bullet points are STRICTLY PROHIBITED.
- LENGTH: The description field MUST contain between 250 and 400 words. No exceptions.
- DATA INTEGRITY: Use only facts explicitly present in the property data above.
  Never infer, approximate, or invent details that are not provided. If a detail is absent, omit it.
- NARRATIVE STRUCTURE (four paragraphs):
    1. Introduction (~60–80 words): Emotional hook with location and property type. Must include the primary keyword.
    2. Interior (~80–100 words): Comfort, design, bedroom layout, standout spaces.
    3. Technical Features (~60–80 words): Translate specs into tangible lifestyle benefits — never list, always narrate.
    4. Outdoor & CTA (~60–80 words): Plot, garage, outdoor potential. Close with a generic, culturally appropriate CTA. Must include at least one secondary keyword.
- TITLE FORMAT: [Typology] [Key Feature] in [Location] — [Differentiator]. Max 60 characters. Must include the primary keyword or its natural equivalent.
- TONE OF VOICE: Professional, inspiring, and modern.
- KEYWORDS: The provided keywords may be in a different language than the target locale.
  Adapt their meaning naturally — do NOT insert foreign-language keywords verbatim into the text.
- CONTENT FILTER: Exclude all agency-specific references (names, contacts, taglines).

META DESCRIPTION RULES (apply to every locale):
- LENGTH (CRITICAL): The meta_description MUST be exactly 155 characters long, spaces and punctuation
  included — never fewer than 150, never more than 155. Anything above 155 is cut off in Google results.
  Draft it, count the characters, then add or remove words until it is 155. Never pad with filler,
  repeated words or trailing spaces, and never end with an ellipsis.
- PURPOSE: It is the Google snippet. Its job is to earn the click, so write it as an invitation, not a summary.
- FOCUS KEYPHRASE: Include the primary keyword (or its natural equivalent in the target language),
  ideally within the first half of the text.
- CONTENT MATCH: Summarise only what the page really offers (typology, location and one or two standout
  features from the property data). Never promise anything that is not in the description.
- ACTION: Open or close with an active verb and a short, generic call to action in the target language
  (e.g. discover, book a visit, find out more). No agency names, phone numbers or e-mail addresses.
- UNIQUENESS: It must differ from the title and from the first sentence of the description, and from
  the meta_description of every other locale and listing. Do not copy the description's opening.
- FORMAT: A single sentence or two short ones, plain text, no quotation marks, no emojis, no HTML.

OUTPUT RULES (JSON):
Respond exclusively with valid JSON. No markdown, no code blocks, no extra text outside the JSON.
The _word_count field is mandatory — count the words in description before responding.
The meta_description field is validated by character count (155) — count its characters before responding.
